# circleci_deploy_environments (Data Source)

Fetches every CircleCI deploy/release environment in an organization. Environments are declared in a
project's `.circleci/config.yml` (the `environment` key on a deploy job) rather than created through the
API, so this is read-only.

Pagination is followed internally, so the result covers every environment rather than one page.

## Availability

| | |
| --- | --- |
| **CircleCI Cloud** | Yes |
| **CircleCI Server** | No — deploy/release tracking is not deployed on CircleCI Server. Using this data source with `deployment = "server"` reports an explicit error. |
| **API** | `GET /api/v2/deploy/environments` |
| **Organization type** | Any. |
| **Token** | Any valid API token. |

-> **Members are a separate concern.** Use [`circleci_deploy_environment`](deploy_environment) to fetch one
environment by id, e.g. after looking its id up here by name.

